WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
First came the age of the Great Ones.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.220
They were mysterious, powerful beings,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.580
each one of them completely unique from
the last.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.820
Then, came the age of the Pthumerians.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.000
The Great Ones once lived alongside the Pthumerians

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.840
but eventually ascended to a higher realm,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.840
leaving the Pthumerians behind.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.700
Finally, came the age of man.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.020
A group of whom discovered the tombs of the Great Ones

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.780
and the Pthumerians who now guarded them.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:35.060
These were the Byrgenwerth scholars, a group devoted to seeking the truth.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.700
They burrowed deep into this world that they
didn't understand.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.100
Uncovering relics, rituals

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.059
and a race that had not been disturbed for a very long time.

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:50.370
Most importantly, though, they stumbled upon a substance called "the old blood".

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:53.289
This blood was incredibly powerful;

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:56.660
as a transfusion with it could cure any illness.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.340
This blood split the ranks of the Byrgenwerth scholars,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.020
for they could not agree on how it was to be used.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.360
The head of the scholars, a man named Willem,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.920
believed that humanity would be undone by the blood.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.660
"Our eyes have yet to open", he said.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.950
So we should fear it.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.740
Other scholars disagreed. Probably thinking him cowardly.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.990
One man, Lawrence, was much more headstrong than his mentor.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.420
He disagreed with Willem. Abandoned him and went on to found the Healing Church.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.600
A society built upon the use of the old blood.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.340
But there was a third man who betrayed the Byrgenwerth scholars.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.280
He stole what the scholars considered
forbidden blood

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.180
and took it far away to the nobles of Cainhurst Castle.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.620
A man named Alfred tells us this:

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:52.030
"Once, a scholar betrayed his fellows at Byrgenwerth..."

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:56.620
"and brought forbidden blood back with him to Cainhurst Castle."

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.930
"It was there that the first of the inhuman Vilebloods was born."

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:08.460
"The Vilebloods are fiendish creatures who threaten the purity of the Church's blood healing."

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.640
"The Ruler of the Vilebloods is still alive today."

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:21.780
And so, to honor my master's wishes, I search, for the path to Cainhurst Castle."

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.540
The people of Cainhurst were proud and Noble

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.100
with a society made up of three tiers:

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.560
At the bottom were the servants and the Knights.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.080
Above them with the nobles; indulgent and arrogant.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.420
And above them all was one, the Queen.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.360
This Queen received the forbidden blood that was stolen from Byrgenwerth

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.820
and became what Alfred calls a Vileblood

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.880
From here, Cainhurst begins to parallel Yharnam in many ways:

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.060
for example, beasts appear

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.500
which are dealt with by the Knights of Cainhurst.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:02.540
The Queen gives employee to hunters who hunt not beasts, but other hunters.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.500
These are her blood hunters who seek blood dregs to feed their beloved Queen

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.420
so that she may one day bear a child of blood.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.980
The Vilebloods become the sworn enemies of the church, for as far as we know,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:23.120
Yharnam and Cainhurst are the only two places with two different strains of the old blood.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.460
It was only natural that they would become rivals.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:32.680
So, the church forms a group called the Executioners, headed by Master Logarius.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.080
The Executioners were zealots

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.820
and existed for the sole purpose of destroying impurity wherever it was found.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.940
Through multiple generations

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.560
they searched for the Vilebloods of Cainhurst Castle.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.470
Eventually they found them

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.310
and departed in force to exact their vengeance.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:04:00.530
"In his time, Master Logarius led his executioners into Cainhurst Castle to cleanse it of the Vilebloods."

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.480
"But all did not go well"

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:07.060
"and Master Logarius became a blessed anchor, "

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.600
"guarding us from evil..."

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.420
"Tragic, tragic times..."

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:18.180
"that Master Logarius should be abandoned in the accursed domain of the Vilebloods."

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.180
I must free him,"

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.880
"so that he may be properly honored in martyrdom."

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.000
Problem is, Alfred does not know how to
get to Cainhurst...

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.600
Yet, in Iosefka's clinic,

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.340
in the clinic where we first awoke

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.940
there's a curious invitation in the back room,

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:46.240
"An old blood-stained summons, inviting an honored guest to the forsaken Castle Cainhurst."

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.580
"Rather bafflingly, it is addressed to you."

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.390
Perhaps it's why we even came to Yhanam in the first place.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:57.890
Do not hesitate; the stagecoach leaves from Hemwick crossing."

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.640
While we're in Cainhurst, we can attempt to clarify where good and evil lie.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.370
Logarius, leader of the executioners, once said:

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.720
"Acts of goodness are not always wise"

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.610
"and acts of evil are not always foolish,"

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.820
"but regardless, we shall always strive to be good."

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.460
But who is Logarius to label good and evil?

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.630
The world is not black and white,

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.210
yet his judgment led to the slaughter of the people of Cainhurst.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.760
So, did these people deserve to be slaughtered?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.820
We arrive and the first thing we notice is that the beasts here are different.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.270
Very few are wolf-like like those in Yharnam

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.390
and in fact, they appear to have evolved according to their environment.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.000
Blood lickers roam, bloating themselves

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:46.190
and the corpses of the fallen that lie beneath the snow

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.690
and gargoyles imitate the architecture,

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:50.890
patiently waiting for their prey.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:56.260
In the halls of Cainhurst roam the ghosts of nobles; undying and ethereal.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:01.980
Upon the tallest tower of Cainhurst we find Logarius, alone.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:07.660
Logarius and his executioners slaughtered every Vileblood noble until one remained:

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:08.680
the Queen.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:13.000
To his despair, Logarius discovered that the Queen was immortal.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.880
She could be rendered, crushed and broken.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.820
But there was always the threat that her flesh would reform,

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.680
so he took the only option available to him.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.400
He donned at the Old King's Crown, a powerful heirloom of Cainhurst.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.440
It allowed him to hide Cainhurst Castle

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.520
and the Queen away from the world.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.080
So that no one would ever stumble upon the last Vileblood.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.860
We murder the withered Logarius and we are granted audience

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.500
with Queen Annalise.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:42.920
"Visitor…"

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.120
"I claim no subjects,"

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.520
"but here lieth Our throne."

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.340
"Kneel afore us…"

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.600
"…or get thee gone."

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.120
"Kneel."

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.920
"Visitor… Moon-scented hunter…"

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.380
"I am Annalise, Queen of Castle Cainhurst."

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:21.440
"Ruler of the Vilebloods, and sworn enemy of the church."

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:26.060
"Yet, Our people are murdered,"

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.280
"and We are prisoner to this wretched mask."

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.720
"What is it thou’rt in search of?"

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.980
It appears that if you were invited to Cainhurst,

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.140
you will always be able to find it.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.840
"Ah-hah! Is that... the sigil of Cainhurst?"

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:52.800
"I've heard tell of Cainhurst nobles, and their amusingly pompous invitations."

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:56.570
"Wonderful! I thank you profusely..."

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:59.710
"I feel my master's hand at work."

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:06.380
"Praise the good blood! And let us cleanse these tarnished streets."

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.760
The order of the executioners believe in martyrdom

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:15.410
That is, they believe in suffering or
dying for a holy cause.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.850
"Martyr" Logarius suffers here on his frozen throne,

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:22.100
to keep the world safe from a perceived evil.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.040
But it cannot be considered absolute martyrdom,

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.720
for the Queen remains alive.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.300
As does Logarius.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.220
Alfred deeply desires to kill this woman,

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:34.220
and perhaps even his master as well.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:39.160
These deaths would allow his idol to pass into legend as a true martyr

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.100
who died for the Greater Good.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:46.580
"Master, look! I've done it, I've done it!"

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:53.980
"I smashed and pounded and grounded this rotten siren into fleshy pink pulp!"

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.240
"There, you filthy monstrosity!"

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.300
"What good's your immortality now!"

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.300
"Try stirring up trouble in this sorry state!"

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:12.900
"All mangled and twisted, with every inside on the outside, for all the world to see!"

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:30.140
"Oh, you, is it? Look at this! Thanks to you, I've done it!"

00:09:30.769 --> 00:09:33.200
"Well? Isn't it wonderful?"

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.940
"Now Master can be canonized as a true martyr!"

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.040
Ironically, Alfred coming here and killing the Queen

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.060
would have run counter to Logarius' wishes.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.540
The queen is undying, so without a guardian,

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.240
there's always the risk that she could rise again.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.680
That is why Logarius stood guard here for all these years.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.380
Yet, of course, acts of goodness are not always wise.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:06.460
So Alfred kills himself so that he can become a martyr,

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:10.200
along with his beloved master. And as Alfred lies dead,

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.480
we take the flesh of the Queen and resurrect her

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.560
in a world now devoid of executioners,

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.440
so that the Vilebloods may rise again.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:24.380
"Well, well… An odd hunter thou art indeed…"

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.720
"We’ve tired of these piteous nights…"

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:37.420
"Share in Our plight, and take oath against the church."

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.740
"Drink deep of Our blood."

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.400
"Feel the spreading corruption burn."

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.300
"Now, thou’rt too a Vileblood."

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.110
"We two,"

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.560
"the very last on this earth."

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.880
"We await thy return."

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.360
For the honor of Cainhurst.

